 diciembre se ajustan a prioridades anuales.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 42 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 10.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.6 to 6.0. December accounts for 12% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,550 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. These stats reflect patterns, like market rates or budget constraints, that don't indicate wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts were for the same need. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service. Contract [1] could indicate a trend if it's part of a larger pattern.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["j85lvrn%2Brz29Hd5zqvq9cg%3D%3D","7bcBP%2B3CJaf%2B3JAijKO%2Bkg%3D%3D","55DJp2DAq5zCfVQHDepjGQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}